                <pb facs="0245" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24 Raw Materials/86: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-26T12:00:00+01:00">April 26,
                        1939—noon</date>.]<lb/>[Received April 26—9:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>558. Thank you for your telegram 293, April 25, 5 p.m., with which I could not
                    agree more. I shall certainly do everything I can to put this across.</p>
                <p>In the meantime it would be helpful if I could have for my own background
                    information an idea of the dimensions of the deal you would like; what have you
                    in mind as to the amount of rubber and tin we would want to have?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
